ment Requirement that must be deleted."},"SystemAnnotations":[],"CustomAnnotations":[],"TagAnnotations":[],"_text":"Id","Siemens.SimaticIT.DSL.Plugin.ILeafNode.Text":"Id"},{"$id":"6441","$type":"DslKeywordNode","Text":"AS","Children":[],"Name":"Keyword","ScriptInfo":{"$ref":"4801"},"SystemAnnotations":[],"CustomAnnotations":[],"TagAnnotations":[],"_text":"AS","Siemens.SimaticIT.DSL.Plugin.ILeafNode.Text":"AS"},{"$id":"6442","$type":"DslCommandPropertyTypeTree","Children":[{"$id":"6443","$type":"DslTerminalNode","Text":"Guid","FullInfo":"Guid","InfoMap":{"$id":"6444","FullIdObj":{"$id":"6445","$type":"IdentificableTypeSystem","Name":"Guid","FullInfo":"Guid","TypeResolved":""}},"FullIdObj":{"$ref":"6445"},"Children":[],"Name":"SimpleSystemTypeNode","ScriptInfo":{"$ref":"4801"},"SystemAnnotations":[],"CustomAnnotations":[],"TagAnnotations":[],"Line":434,"CharPositionInLine":10,"_text":"Guid","Siemens.SimaticIT.DSL.Plugin.ILeafNode.Text":"Guid"}],"Name":"CommandPropertyType","ScriptInfo":{"$ref":"4801"},"SystemAnnotations":[],"CustomAnnotations":[],"TagAnnotations":[]}],"Name":"PropertyTree","ScriptInfo":{"$ref":"4801"},"SystemAnnotations":[],"CustomAnnotations":[],"TagAnnotations":[]}]}],"Name":"Input declaration commands","ScriptInfo":{"$ref":"4801"},"SystemAnnotations":[],"CustomAnnotations":[],"TagAnnotations":[]}],"Name":"CommandDeclaration","ScriptInfo":{"$ref":"4801"},"SystemAnnotations":[],"CustomAnnotations":[],"TagAnnotations":[]},{"$id":"6446","$type":"DslCommandDeclarationTree","HasInput":true,"Children":[{"$id":"6447","$type":"DslKeywordNode","Text":"COMMAND","Children":[],"Name":"Keyword","ScriptInfo":{"$ref":"4801"},"SystemAnnotations":[],"CustomAnnotations":[],"TagAnnotations":[],"_text":"COMMAND","Siemens.SimaticIT.DSL.Plugin.ILeafNode.Text":"COMMAND"},{"$id":"6448","$type":"DslTerminalNode","Text":"UpdateWorkOrderOperationEquipmentRequirement","FullInfo":"Siemens.SimaticIT.UAPI.OperationalData.PICore_OP.OPModel.Commands.UpdateWorkOrderOperationEquipmentRequirement","InfoMap":{"$id":"6449","FullIdObj":{"$id":"6450","$type":"IdentificableObject","Guid":"e03776cf-8b0c-493a-933e-36e02dad0e51","Name":"UpdateWorkOrderOperationEquipmentRequirement","FullInfo":"Siemens.SimaticIT.UAPI.OperationalData.PICore_OP.OPModel.Commands.UpdateWorkOrderOperationEquipmentRequirement","TypeResolved":"","_project":{"$ref":"12"},"_domain":{"$ref":"4804"}}},"FullIdObj":{"$ref":"6450"},"Children":[],"Name":"CommandName","ScriptInfo":{"$ref":"4801"},"Documentation":{"$id":"6451","$type":"DslTerminalNode","Text":"Updates a Work Order Operation Equipment Requirement. \r\nAssigns the value of Sequence, RequirementTag and PlannedEquipmentNId Properties from the given command inputs: if an empty value is given, it deletes an existing value.  \r\nThis is not applied for the value of the arguments EquipmentGroupNId and EquipmentNId: an empty value does not delete an existing value. \r\nOptionally flags the Equipment Requirement setting is as Main. This applies only to Equipment Requirement that specifies the EquipmentGroupNId. Any other Equipment Requirement previously set as Main will have the flag reset. \r\nWarning: if you define both the EquipmentNId and EquipmentGroupNId arguments: the command verifies if the piece of Equipment defined by the EquipmentNId is part of Equipment Group defined by the EquipmentGroupNId. If it is not the case, it throws the error 10861. \r\nChecks if the given Equipment Requirement Id exists. Throws the error 10300 otherwise. \r\nChecks if the PlannedEquipmentNId, EquipmentNId, or EquipmentGroupNId exist. Throws the error 10996 otherwise. \r\nChecks if the value of the PlannedSetupStartTime is inferior to the value of the PlannedSetupEndTime. Throws the error 11315 otherwise. \r\nIf the \"IsMain\" property is set equal to True, checks if the Equipment Group identifier is specified, If not error -10899 is returned; ","FullInfo":"Updates a Work Order Operation Equipment Requirement. \r\nAssigns the value of Sequence, RequirementTag and PlannedEquipmentNId Properties from the given command inputs: if an empty value is given, it deletes an existing value.  \r\nThis is not applied for the value of the arguments EquipmentGroupNId and EquipmentNId: an empty value does not delete an existing value. \r\nOptionally flags the Equipment Requirement setting is as Main. This applies only to Equipment Requirement that specifies the EquipmentGroupNId. Any other Equipment Requirement previously set as Main will have the flag reset. \r\nWarning: if you define both the EquipmentNId and EquipmentGroupNId arguments: the command verifies if the piece of Equipment defined by the EquipmentNId is part of Equipment Group defined by the EquipmentGroupNId. If it is not the case, it throws the error 10861. \r\nChecks if the given Equipment Requirement Id exists. Throws the error 10300 otherwise. \r\nChecks if the PlannedEquipmentNId, EquipmentNId, or EquipmentGroupNId exist. Throws the error 10996 otherwise. \r\nChecks if the value of the PlannedSetupStartTime is inferior to the value of the PlannedSetupEndTime. Throws the error 11315 otherwise. \r\nIf the \"IsMain\" property is set equal to True, checks if the Equipment Group identifier is specified, If not error -10899 is returned; ","InfoMap":{"$id":"6452","FullIdObj":{"$id":"6453","$type":"IdentificableText","Name":"Updates a Work Order Operation Equipment Requirement. \r\nAssigns the value of Sequence, RequirementTag and PlannedEquipmentNId Properties from the given command inputs: if an empty value is given, it deletes an existing value.  \r\nThis is not applied for the value of the arguments EquipmentGroupNId and EquipmentNId: an empty value does not delete an existing value. \r\nOptionally flags the Equipment Requirement setting is as Main. This applies only to Equipment Requirement that specifies the EquipmentGroupNId. Any other Equipment Requirement previously set as Main will have the flag reset. \r\nWarning: if you define both the EquipmentNId and EquipmentGroupNId arguments: the command verifies if the piece of Equipment defined by the EquipmentNId is part of Equipment Group defined by the EquipmentGroupNId. If it is not the case, it throws the error 10861. \r\nChecks if the given Equipment Requirement Id exists. Throws the error 10300 otherwise. \r\nChecks if the PlannedEquipmentNId, EquipmentNId, or EquipmentGroupNId exist. Throws the error 10996 otherwise. \r\nChecks if the value of the PlannedSetupStartTime is inferior to the value of the PlannedSetupEndTime. Throws the error 11315 otherwise. \r\nIf the \"IsMain\" property is set equal to True, checks if the Equipment Group identifier is specified, If not error -10899 is returned; ","FullInfo":"Updates a Work Order Operation Equipment Requirement. \r\nAssigns the value of Sequence, RequirementTag and PlannedEquipmentNId Properties from the given command inputs: if an empty value is given, it deletes an existing value.  \r\nThis is not applied for the value of the arguments EquipmentGroupNId and EquipmentNId: an empty value does not delete an existing value. \r\nOptionally flags the Equipment Requirement setting is as Main. This applies only to Equipment Requirement that specifies the EquipmentGroupNId. Any other Equipment Requirement previously set as Main will have the flag reset. \r\nWarning: if you define both the EquipmentNId and EquipmentGroupNId arguments: the command verifies if the piece of Equipment defined by the EquipmentNId is part of Equipment Group defined by the EquipmentGroupNId. If it is not the case, it throws the error 10861. \r\nChecks if the given Equipment Requirement Id exists. Throws the error 10300 otherwise. \r\nChecks if the PlannedEquipmentNId, EquipmentNId, or EquipmentGroupNId exist. Throws the error 10996 otherwise. \r\nChecks if the value of the PlannedSetupStartTime is inferior to the value of the PlannedSetupEndTime. Throws the error 11315 otherwise. \r\nIf the \"IsMain\" property is set equal to True, checks if the Equipment Group identifier is specified, If not error -10899 is returned; ","TypeResolved":""}},"FullIdObj":{"$ref":"6453"},"Children":[],"Name":"Documentation","SystemAnnotations":[],"CustomAnnotations":[],"TagAnnotations":[],"_text":"Updates a Work Order Operation Equipment Requirement. \r\nAssigns the value of Sequence, RequirementTag and PlannedEquipmentNId Properties from the given command inputs: if an empty value is given, it deletes an existing value.  \r\nThis is not applied for the value of the arguments EquipmentGroupNId and EquipmentNId: an empty value does not delete an existing value. \r\nOptionally flags the Equipment Requirement setting is as Main. This applies only to Equipment Requirement that specifies the EquipmentGroupNId. Any other Equipment Requirement previously set as Main will have the flag reset. \r\nWarning: if you define both the EquipmentNId and EquipmentGroupNId arguments: the command verifies if the piece of Equipment defined by the EquipmentNId is part of Equipment Group defined by the EquipmentGroupNId. If it is not the case, it throws the error 10861. \r\nChecks if the given Equipment Requirement Id exists. Throws the error 10300 otherwise. \r\nChecks if the PlannedEquipmentNId, EquipmentNId, or EquipmentGroupNId exist. Throws the error 10996 otherwise. \r\nChecks if the value of the PlannedSetupStartTime is inferior to the value of the PlannedSetupEndTime. Throws the error 11315 otherwise. \r\nIf the \"IsMain\" property is set equal to True, checks if the Equipment Group identifier is specified, If not error -10899 is returned; ","Siemens.SimaticIT.DSL.Plugin.ILeafNode.Text":"Updates a Work Order Operation Equipment Requirement. \r\nAssigns the value of Sequence, RequirementTag and PlannedEquipmentNId Properties from the given command inputs: if an empty value is given, it deletes an existing value.  \r\nThis is not applied for the value of the arguments EquipmentGroupNId and EquipmentNId: an empty value does not delete an exis